# Prezi

> Prezi is a presentation platform built for engagement. Create presentations with AI, engage audiences live with polls, quizzes, and Q&A, then share a single link people can revisit and respond to after the session ends.

Prezi helps presenters hold the room, make ideas click, and keep them alive after everyone leaves — so what you say is what they remember. Over 170 million people across 195+ countries have created more than 500 million presentations with Prezi.

## How it works

1. **Start where you are**: Bring a deck you already have (PowerPoint, Google Slides, Canva, PDF, Word) or describe what you need and Prezi AI drafts it.
2. **Keep attention**: Present on a zoomable canvas that shows how ideas connect, so the audience follows the shape of the argument — not just the next slide.
3. **Engage**: Drop in live polls, quizzes, and Q&A that everyone joins from their phone via QR code — no app install needed. Passive watching turns into active thinking.
4. **Share anywhere**: Send a link, video, or podcast afterward, then see what landed with quiz results and end-of-session feedback.

## Key capabilities

- **AI presentation creation**: Describe your topic and Prezi drafts a complete presentation.
- **Zoomable canvas**: A non-linear presentation format that shows relationships between ideas.
- **Live audience engagement**: Polls, quizzes, word clouds, Q&A, and feedback — audiences join via QR code on any device.
- **Import existing decks**: Bring in PowerPoint, Google Slides, Canva exports, PDF, or Word documents.
- **Post-session content**: Every presentation becomes a shareable link with narrated video, podcast, self-paced quiz, and AI-powered Q&A from the content.
- **Analytics**: Quiz and poll results, audience questions, ratings, and feedback digests.
- **Brand customization**: Apply brand colors, fonts, and logos across presentations.
- **SCORM export**: Package presentations for LMS delivery.

## Who uses Prezi

- **Trainers**: Onboarding and corporate training with built-in participation and proof of completion.
- **Teachers**: K-12 lessons with active participation from every seat and student review tools.
- **Professors**: Lectures that work in-person, online, and async, with comprehension data.
- **Teams**: Internal presentations and all-hands with live engagement.

